=== A2.19 K6-1 Memory Syscalls Evidence Log ===
Date: 2026-11-06
Agent: antigravity (chat A2)

1. IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY
- kernel/src/paging.rs:
  * Added unmap_user_page(pml4_phys: u64, vpage: u64) -> Option<u64> to unmap user PTE, free physical frame to PMM, and execute invlpg if active CR3 matches.
  * Added translate_cr3(cr3_phys: u64, va: u64) -> Option<u64> to walk arbitrary process 4-level page tables and resolve virtual-to-physical address mapping.
- kernel/src/proc.rs:
  * Defined user address space layout:
    USER_CODE_VADDR = 0x0040_0000
    USER_HEAP_BASE = 0x0050_0000
    USER_HEAP_MAX = 0x0070_0000
    USER_MMAP_BASE = 0x0070_0000
    USER_MMAP_MAX = 0x007E_F000
    USER_GUARD_PAGE = 0x007F_E000 (strictly unmapped)
    USER_STACK_PAGE = 0x007F_F000
    USER_STACK_TOP = 0x0080_0000
  * Added Process fields brk and mmap_cur, initialized to USER_HEAP_BASE and USER_MMAP_BASE.
  * Implemented sys_brk(new_brk: u64) -> i64 (query brk on 0, expand/shrink heap with page allocation and unmapping).
  * Implemented sys_mmap(addr: u64, len: u64, prot: u64) -> i64 (anonymous memory allocation).
  * Implemented sys_munmap(addr: u64, len: u64) -> i64.
  * Wired SYS_BRK (12, alias 7), SYS_MMAP (9, alias 8), SYS_MUNMAP (11, alias 10) in syscall_dispatch.
  * Added Ring 3 test payloads: mem_alloc_user_entry, guard_page_user_entry, mem_owner_user_entry, mem_snooper_user_entry.
- kernel/src/trustselftest.rs:
  * Added Test 11a: Ring 3 mem_alloc expands heap via sys_brk, writes to heap, maps anonymous memory via sys_mmap, writes to mmap, verifies values, unmaps with sys_munmap, shrinks heap with sys_brk, exits 42.
  * Added Test 11b: Ring 3 guard_probe accesses stack guard page at 0x007F_E000. Asserts #PF (vector 14), CR2 = 0x007F_E000, P=0, U=1, and process termination.
  * Added Test 11c: Process A (mem_owner) writes secret 0x5345_4352_4554_3121 to 0x0050_0000 and exits. Process B (mem_snooper) attempts to access 0x0050_0000 in its own address space, faulting with #PF (vector 14), CR2 = 0x0050_0000, P=0, U=1. Asserts Process A's secret remains intact via translate_cr3.

